<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - ELECTRICIDAD CARACAS CUT.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - ELECTRICIDAD CARACAS CUT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresdner Kleinwort Benson said on Tuesday it cut its rating on the shares of Electricidad de Caracas to reduce from hold.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Cecilia Tam said in a research note that the Venezuelan electricity company's shares have risen 145 percent in U.S. dollar terms over the past year.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Although often held as a proxy for the Venezuelan market, we believe that EDC is currently overvalued vis-a-vis both the Latam power sector and local market,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- The stock closed at 812 bolivares in Caracas.</p>
<p>((Wall Street desk 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
